    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0440" n="296" xml:id="pg296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/234: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-21T11:00:00+08:00">August 21, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 21—10:31 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>742. My 739, August 20, noon.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d188-f1"/> Following from
                    American Consul at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 20, 1 p.m. Customs reports from Pogranichnaya states Tungning
                            occupied by regular Soviet troops; other reports state it is occupied by
                            irregular troops consisting of Koreans, Buriats and Magyars who form
                            front-line Soviet troops. Locomotive mail train near Pogranichnaya,
                            August 20th, blown up by bomb but train not damaged. Chinese
                            Commissioner of Foreign Affairs [at] Taheiho has telegraphed all consuls
                            complaining against raids into Chinese territory by alleged forces of
                            Soviet side whom he accuses of violating international law.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="62" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it repeated telegram of August 19, from the Consul at Harbin, <ref
                        target="#pg286">p. 286</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
